{
  "name": "Score new Shopify stores from Apify and route hot leads to Sheets and Slack",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Score new Shopify stores from Apify and route hot leads to Sheets and Slack\n\nShopify app developers, agencies and freelancers who sell to new merchants and want a short, ranked list of fresh stores every morning instead of a raw dump.\n\n### How it works\n1. A **Schedule Trigger** runs daily and **Set your settings** holds your targets.\n2. An **HTTP Request** runs the New Shopify Stores Pre-Launch Radar Actor on Apify (public Certificate Transparency logs, DNS, store metadata).\n3. **Skip stores already seen** drops domains handled in earlier runs.\n4. **Score each store** gives 0–10 points: pre-launch, target niche, target country, small catalog, ships abroad, young domain, with the reasons in plain words.\n5. Every store is logged in Google Sheets (updated by domain).\n6. A **Switch** sends hot stores to Slack one by one and bundles warm ones into one digest.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create an Apify account and a **Header Auth** credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and Slack.\n3. In **Set your settings**, paste your sheet URL and Slack channel, then set your niches and countries.\n4. Run once (sample data is pinned), unpin, activate.\n\nApify account (billed per store returned, $0.02 each; `maxItems` caps every run), a Google Sheet with a `Stores` tab, a Slack workspace.\n\n### Customization\n- Change the points or add rules in the **Score each store** code.\n- Raise or lower `hotScore` to control how many alerts you get.\n- Swap Slack for email, or Sheets for your CRM.\n\nBusiness-level public data only: no emails, phones or personal names. Not affiliated with Shopify Inc. Disclosure: I built the Apify Actor used here.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 640
      },
      "id": "0a84de00-82f1-5849-9967-f388084bbb80",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -720,
        0
      ]
    },
